      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenViking is an open-source context database that solves the challenge of managing complex information for AI agents by organizing memory, resources, and skills through a file system paradigm. Its technical innovation lies in enabling hierarchical context delivery and self-evolving capabilities, allowing agents to access and update information efficiently. Developers can integrate it into agent frameworks like OpenClaw to build more capable AI systems that learn and adapt over time through structured context management.",
        "zh": "OpenViking 是一个专为 AI 智能体设计的开源上下文数据库，它通过文件系统范式统一管理智能体所需的内存、资源和技能，解决了复杂信息组织的难题。其技术核心在于支持分层上下文传递和自进化能力，使智能体能够高效访问和更新信息。开发者可以将其集成到 OpenClaw 等智能体框架中，构建能够通过结构化上下文管理持续学习和适应的更强大 AI 系统，为实际应用提供灵活、可扩展的解决方案。",
        "es": "OpenViking is an open-source context database that solves the challenge of managing complex information for AI agents by organizing memory, resources, and skills through a file system paradigm. Its technical innovation lies in enabling hierarchical context delivery and self-evolving capabilities, allowing agents to access and update information efficiently. Developers can integrate it into agent frameworks like OpenClaw to build more capable AI systems that learn and adapt over time through structured context management.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "OpenViking stands out for agent, agentic-rag, and ai-agents in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "OpenViking is an open-source context database that solves the challenge of managing complex information for AI agents by organizing memory, resources, and skills through a file system paradigm. Its technical innovation lies in enabling hierarchical context delivery and self-evolving capabilities, allowing agents to access and update information efficiently. Developers can integrate it into agent frameworks like OpenClaw to build more capable AI systems that learn and adapt over time through structured context management.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/volcengine/OpenViking for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
