      "summaries": {
        "en": "Dimos is a Python-based dimensional framework that provides a structured approach to managing complex data relationships and transformations in AI systems. It introduces a novel dimensional abstraction layer that separates data representation from processing logic, enabling more modular and maintainable code architectures. Developers can use Dimos to build scalable data pipelines, implement custom transformations, and experiment with different dimensional representations for tasks like feature engineering, model interpretability, or multi-modal data integration.",
        "zh": "Dimos是一个基于Python的维度框架，专门解决AI系统中复杂数据关系和转换的结构化管理问题。它通过创新的维度抽象层，将数据表示与处理逻辑分离，使代码架构更加模块化和可维护。该框架的核心在于将高维数据操作封装为可组合的维度变换，让开发者能够专注于业务逻辑而非底层实现。你可以用它构建可扩展的数据流水线，实现自定义特征转换，或为多模态数据集成、模型可解释性等任务设计灵活的维度表示方案。",
        "es": "Dimos is a Python-based dimensional framework that provides a structured approach to managing complex data relationships and transformations in AI systems. It introduces a novel dimensional abstraction layer that separates data representation from processing logic, enabling more modular and maintainable code architectures. Developers can use Dimos to build scalable data pipelines, implement custom transformations, and experiment with different dimensional representations for tasks like feature engineering, model interpretability, or multi-modal data integration.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "dimos gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Dimos is a Python-based dimensional framework that provides a structured approach to managing complex data relationships and transformations in AI systems. It introduces a novel dimensional abstraction layer that separates data representation from processing logic, enabling more modular and maintainable code architectures. Developers can use Dimos to build scalable data pipelines, implement custom transformations, and experiment with different dimensional representations for tasks like feature engineering, model interpretability, or multi-modal data integration.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/dimensionalOS/dimos for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
